From 6ee692ee3a6e36ded8a8e1417de9540f887b888c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:25:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10948/11362] Report a rejected artifact with the reason it was
 actually rejected

_artifact_is_finished refuses an artifact for two independent reasons -- a
bootstrap status, or a verdict the classifier will not trust -- and
_log_experiment_completion reported both as
artifact_not_updated_past_bootstrap, which asserts the artifact was never
written.

Of exp6952 that was simply false. The V608 capstone burned all three attempts
under that message while its artifact was written every time, complete, clean,
and rejected for declaring verdict_class partial. An outer-loop session spent an
hour chasing a bootstrap-write bug that did not exist, and found the real cause
only by calling _verdict_is_untrustworthy by hand.

Splits the reason out as _artifact_unfinished_reason returning (token, detail),
with _artifact_is_finished kept as a bool wrapper because three callers and a
test module read it that way. A verdict rejection now logs
artifact_verdict_not_terminal and names both the verdict and the declared class,
so the next reader can act without opening the artifact. The bootstrap token
keeps its exact old spelling: log greps and this file's own incident history
depend on that string, and renaming it would have been a second bug wearing the
first one's clothes.

REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3 with two scenarios. Six tests. Mutation-proven by
collapsing the two tokens back into one, which goes RED, then restoring
byte-identically, which goes GREEN. The 29 existing conductor tests still pass,
including REQ-CONDUCTOR-FINISHED-1's terminal-blocked case, which the refactor
had to preserve.

The test fixture monkeypatches PROJECT_ROOT rather than writing into the real
tree, because a test that mutates tracked state is forbidden here and because an
absolute path makes the function return None, which reads as a pass. Both
mistakes were made while investigating this bug.

